---
title: "accrue_interest (Current Finance - Reserve Interest Model)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_updated: last_updated == now?
    q_check_updated --> q_skip: already accrued this block; return early
    q_check_updated --> q_calc_factor: simple_interest_factor = interest_rate * (now - last_updated)
    q_calc_factor --> q_calc_accrued: interest_accumulated = debt * simple_interest_factor
    q_calc_accrued --> q_update_debt: debt = debt + interest_accumulated
    q_update_debt --> q_update_reserve: cash_reserve = cash_reserve + reserve_factor * interest_accumulated
    q_update_reserve --> q_update_index: new_borrow_index = factor * borrow_index_prior + borrow_index_prior
    q_update_index --> q_set_index: borrow_index.set_value(new_borrow_index, now)
    q_set_index --> [*]: return

    note right of q_check_updated
        INV-001: Interest accrual is idempotent within a single timestamp (skip if last_updated == now)
        INV-002: Borrow index is monotonically non-decreasing (enforced by set_value assertion)
    end note

    note right of q_update_index
        INV-003: Simple interest model: new_index = index_prior * (1 + rate * dt)
        INV-004: reserve_factor portion of interest goes to protocol reserve (not lenders)
        INV-005: cash_reserve grows with each accrue; represents protocol-owned share
    end note
